# Keep guides in sync

The Guides section (`/dashboard/knowledge`) is written in `src/lib/knowledge-base/*.ts`.
Guides name exact on-screen labels, tabs, buttons and pages, so UI changes make them wrong.

## When this applies

Any change a user can see: renamed or removed labels, fields, checkboxes, buttons, tabs,
sidebar items, page moves, new features, or changed behaviour (limits, defaults, fees).
Pure refactors, styling and server-only fixes don't need guide changes.

## What to do, in the same commit

1. Search the guides for every old label, route and feature name you touched:
   `rg -n "Show exact stock|tab=payments|Checkout payments" src/lib/knowledge-base`
2. Update matching `steps`, `tips`, `summary`, `keywords` and `ctas`. Use the new label text exactly as it appears on screen.
3. Removed a feature? Delete the step; don't leave "no longer available" notes.
4. Moved a page? Update `ctas[].href`.
5. New user-facing feature? Add a step to the closest article, or a new article in the matching category file with `related` links.
6. Run `npm run test:guides` (checks links, related guides, Start here).

## Report it

End your summary with one line:
- `Guides updated: business-setup.ts (Business details), getting-started.ts`
- or `Guides: no changes needed (internal only)`

## Example

Removed the "Show exact stock publicly" checkbox from Business Details:

```ts
// ❌ left in business-setup.ts
"Tick Show exact stock publicly to show counts instead of Available / Low stock / Sold out.",
// ✅ step deleted, and the summary no longer mentions "stock display"
```
